# Testing and Verification

- Inspect package scripts and existing test conventions before running commands. Prefer the narrowest relevant tests first.
- Test user-visible behavior, authorization boundaries, validation, error handling, provider failures, empty states and important edge cases.
- For job ingestion, test normalization, source provenance, pagination, throttling, retries, stale/expired listings and deduplication false positives.
- For matching and AI, test deterministic baselines, schema validation, privacy routing, provider fallback, quotas, quality fixtures and non-determinism appropriately.
- For resumes, test malformed/large files, extraction correctness, user approval, export and prevention of fabricated fields.
- For marketing pages, verify mobile layouts, semantics, metadata, canonical URLs, sitemap and accessibility.
- Do not weaken/remove tests or snapshot assertions merely to make a suite green. Explain intentional test changes.
- Report exact command, exit status, passed/failed/skipped counts and relevant environment constraints. Do not claim tests were run if they were not.
- A passing unit suite is not proof of end-to-end or production readiness. State verification scope precisely.